{"segs": ["PA_ja_134:0.4"], "en": "4. The Jātaka on Purifying the Meditative Absorptions (Jhānasodhanajātaka):", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_134:1.1"], "en": "“Those who possess perception have fared ill;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_134:1.2"], "en": "those who are without perception have also fared ill.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_134:1.3"], "en": "Avoiding both of these,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_134:1.4"], "en": "that bliss of attainment is free from blemish.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
